laurel 2913: the frame path. The clock of CoreAnimation follows the panel (INTF1 line + frame counter, on by default, kill switch sweetfb_lock=0; boot 22:08: 57 ticks a second against 60 panel frames). The presenter sleeps to the latch instead of 100 us looks, at priority 92. SWEET FPS keeps its text, its sums now restart with the window (boot 22:08: 14.4 s of waits in a 10 s line). New line LAUREL FRAME per window: tick period, frames/s while moving, gaps by missed panel frames, queue + fence + latch, touch to next flip. RedwoodGPU: the impossible "MHz while busy" is gone, a submission's lock wait and hold, the window server's kernel time. Request 0x7c + kRedwoodAnyLayout: a texture of each plane of an IOSurface (A008, L008, LA08, _RB4). A surface named by a client that is not the window server gets a new seed (kill switch gpuclientseed=0). docs/laurel_sprout/gpu.md "Frame budget".

